window.docContents[64].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalSpqrV1.Core/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalSpqrV1___Core":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalSpqrV1 › Core.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 7 headline theorems depend on it 68 of 133 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (13)abbrev Epochabbrev Secretstructure EpochSecretinductive Directiondef switchdef toI32def fromI32?inductive Errordef isStateDecodeinductive SpqrPanicdef inzdef isNonZerodef compare\n\nSPQR V1: shared core types (src/lib.rs) and constant-time helpers (src/util.rs)Trusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except Direction.A2B and Direction.B2A, which are checked by Lean (see Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md).Shared SPQR V1 types (Epoch, Secret, EpochSecret, Direction with switch and toI32, Error with isStateDecode, SpqrPanic) and constant-time comparison helpers (inz, isNonZero, compare) from spqr (src/lib.rs, src/util.rs).\n\n\n\nCore types from src/lib.rs and src/proto/pq_ratchet.proto\n\nabbrev EpochL32–33 ↗#pub type Epoch = u64 (src/lib.rs:40).\n\nabbrev SecretL35–36 ↗#pub type Secret = Vec<u8> (src/lib.rs:41).\n\nstructure EpochSecretL38–42 ↗#pub struct EpochSecret (src/lib.rs:50–53).\n\ninductive DirectionL44–48 ↗#pub enum Direction (src/proto/pq_ratchet.proto:218–221, src/lib.rs:28, 63–70).\n\n\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 52–54): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalSpqrV1.Direction.A2B, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSpqrV1.Direction.B2A\n\ndef switchL56–58 ↗#\n\ndef toI32L60–63 ↗#Protobuf i32 encoding (0 for a2b, 1 for b2a).\n\ndef fromI32?L65–69 ↗#Direction::try_from(v: i32) (src/proto/pq_ratchet.proto:218–221).\n\n\n\ninductive ErrorL73–91 ↗#pub enum Error (src/lib.rs:96–130).\n\n\n\ndef isStateDecodeL95–97 ↗#\n\n\n\nPanics\n\ninductive SpqrPanicL103–108 ↗#Shared Rust panic sites (compareBounds at src/util.rs:29, or site for cited panics).\n\nsrc/util.rs\n\ndef inzL112–116 ↗#spqr::util::inz(value: u8) -> u8 (src/util.rs:7–13).\n\ndef isNonZeroL118–119 ↗#\n\ndef compareL121–127 ↗#spqr::util::compare(lhs: &[u8], rhs: &[u8]) -> u8 (src/util.rs:25–33): returns 0 iff lhs equals the first lhs.length bytes of rhs, or panics with compareBounds when lhs.length > rhs.length.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalSpqrV1/Core.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalSpqrV1.Core/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalSpqrV1___Core"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Refinement.ElfBinding/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Refinement___ElfBinding":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement › ElfBinding.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 6 headline theorems depend on it 219 of 304 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: none; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (20)def HooksMatchInterpretationdef vec32def InputsEquivdef preKeyOfBody?def PqFieldsMatchdef pqRecvMatchingFieldsModeldef pqInitInputsFabbrev DirsAgreeOnInputabbrev ModelAgreesOnInputdef realCliHooksabbrev RealHooksAgreeOnInputdef HooksMatchPlaceddef elfReldef CliElfProgressdef CompRefinesCliBinarydef RealPrimsMatchdef RealPrimsAdmissibledef elfRelRealdef CliElfProgressRealdef CompRefinesCliBinaryReal\n\n\n\nELF Binding for CLI RefinementInstantiates CompRefinesCli with the ARM64 ELF run relation (elfRel) using symbol addresses resolved from the ELF's .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs), together with hook-to-symbol and FIPS 197 AES-256 agreement (HooksMatchPlaced), per-call primitive agreement with the executed ELF primitives (RealHooksAgreeOnInput, realCliHooks), and the progress guarantee up to SampleNTT seed divergence (CliElfProgress, DEV-CLI22).\n\n\n\ndef HooksMatchInterpretationL49–69 ↗#Agreement between CliHooks W and ExternInterpretation interp on SHA-256 compression, AES-256-CBC, X25519, and Kyber-1024.\n\n\n\ndef vec32L73–74 ↗#Zero-pads or truncates b to 32 bytes.\n\ndef InputsEquivL76–79 ↗#Equivalence of CLI Inputs up to directory-snapshot extensionality under filesOf.\n\ndef preKeyOfBody?L81–96 ↗#Extracts PreKeyMessageFields from a pre-key message body when parsePreKey succeeds at version 4 with a 1568-byte Kyber ciphertext prefixed by 0x08.\n\ndef PqFieldsMatchL98–101 ↗#Checks whether an existing session (x, g) matches parsed pre-key fields q on aliceBaseKey and sessionVersion.\n\ndef pqRecvMatchingFieldsModelL103–117 ↗#Model transition for decrypting a parsed pre-key message q against a matching existing session (x, g).\n\ndef pqInitInputsFL119–123 ↗#CLI init inputs for party st over an arbitrary bundle file list files and 192-byte randomness tape t.\n\nabbrev DirsAgreeOnInputL125–136 ↗#Per-call party-directory and spec-domain agreement guard between primitive parameters P and P₀ on input i: on every P-spec-domain party state st and admissible extra-file list extra whose pqInputs matches i, encodeDir P st = encodeDir P₀ st (the stored X25519 public-key files match P₀) and st also lies in PqxdhPartyInSpecDomain P₀ (trivially True when P = P₀). Restricting extra to flat bundleDir files on init and [] otherwise (matching ValidCall) prevents extra from shadowing encodeDir P st entries under last-wins filesOf.\n\nabbrev ModelAgreesOnInputL138–174 ↗#Per-call model-agreement guard between primitive parameters P and P₀ on input i: on every spec-domain CLI transition matching i, the protocol model at P produces the same transition as at P₀. Shared across the linked, closed cryptographic primitives (trivially True when P = P₀).\n\n\n\ndef realCliHooksL178–180 ↗#The closed CLI primitives executed by the linked ELF code (realCrypto and realPqxdhPrims from CliBinaryPq.lean).\n\nabbrev RealHooksAgreeOnInputL182–200 ↗#Per-call domain guard: on every spec-domain transition matching i, the calling party's encoded key files and spec-domain membership (ElfGuard.DirsAgreeOnInput) and the protocol model transition (ElfGuard.ModelAgreesOnInput) at W agree with realCliHooks.* Real-binary instantiation: at W = realCliHooks, RealHooksAgreeOnInput W i holds on every input, so elfRel reduces to runFnToRelation (cliRunElf elf addrs) (no RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter). Admissibility of realCliHooks (RealPrimsAdmissible: ∃ interp, ExternContractsHoldCli interp ∧ RealPrimsMatch interp) is proved by Proven.Refinement.real_prims_admissible, and CompRefinesCliBinaryReal (below) and SignalSessionSecureReal (Symbolic/Specifications/Security/Binary.lean) fix the primitives to realCliHooks via RealPrimsMatch over elfRelReal (dropping the RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter while retaining the CliTraces step guards and InvertsGuarded / CoinsFresh premises).* Non-vacuity and witness interpretations: agreement is required only on reachable trace inputs, so witness interpretations keep real X25519 public keys on the setup secrets while preserving collision-free / synthetic SHA-256 and X25519 laws and lookup-table Kyber / ML-KEM off-trace.\n\ndef HooksMatchPlacedL202–207 ↗#Binary primitive agreement: HooksMatchInterpretation interp W with W.C.E and W.C.D fixed to the closed FIPS 197 AES-256 block cipher (CryptoGames.AES256.aes256Enc, CryptoGames.AES256.aes256Dec) executed by the linked ELF code.\n\ndef elfRelL209–214 ↗#ARM64 process run relation of elf at .symtab-resolved addresses addrs under hooks W, guarded by per-call agreement with the executed primitives (RealHooksAgreeOnInput W i).\n\ndef CliElfProgressL216–232 ↗#Progress (no CPU fault, trap, or non-termination unless the run reaches a non-terminating SampleNTT entry, CliReachesSampleNttStuckElf, DEV-CLI22) on every guarded CliCall (RealHooksAgreeOnInput W i) at any turn reachable from initDirs under elfRel elf addrs: either cliRunElf elf addrs i produces a process outcome, or the run reaches one of the 5 libcrux_ml_kem SampleNTT entry points with a SHAKE-128 matrix seed that never terminates (CliReachesSampleNttStuckElf elf addrs i, DEV-CLI22).\n\ndef CompRefinesCliBinaryL234–242 ↗#Whole-protocol refinement and progress guarantee for ELF image bytes: parses bytes, resolves the 18 panic and 5 SampleNTT addresses from .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs), and asserts CliElfProgress elf addrs and CompRefinesCli HooksMatchPlaced (elfRel elf addrs).\n\nReal-primitive statementsThe statements below fix the CLI primitives to the closed primitives executed by the linked ELF (realCliHooks) instead of quantifying over all agreeing W : CliHooks. The run relation elfRelReal therefore drops the RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter, so CompRefinesCliBinaryReal and SignalSessionSecureReal cover every guarded execution trace of cliRunElf from initDirs (CliTraces still requires ValidCall, InputsFor, and LeaksFrom on every step, and InvertsGuarded and CoinsFresh remain premises). The remaining universal quantifier is over extern interpretations interp that satisfy the symbolic laws (ExternContractsHoldCli) and agree with the real primitives (RealPrimsMatch); RealPrimsAdmissible asserts that such an interp exists, i.e. that the real primitives obey the laws assumed by the symbolic model.\n\ndef RealPrimsMatchL256–259 ↗#Extern interpretation interp agrees with the closed primitives executed by the linked ELF (HooksMatchPlaced interp realCliHooks).\n\ndef RealPrimsAdmissibleL261–264 ↗#The real primitives obey the symbolic laws: some extern interpretation satisfies ExternContractsHoldCli and agrees with realCliHooks.\n\ndef elfRelRealL266–272 ↗#ARM64 process run relation of elf at .symtab-resolved addresses addrs (starting from plain ElfImage.loadState), without the RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter. The primitive parameter is Unit: the ELF executes its own linked primitives (realCliHooks).\n\ndef CliElfProgressRealL274–287 ↗#Progress (no CPU fault, trap, or non-termination unless the run reaches a non-terminating SampleNTT entry, CliReachesSampleNttStuckElf elf addrs i, DEV-CLI22) on every guarded CliCall (ValidCall / InputsFor) at any turn reachable from initDirs under elfRelReal elf addrs (no RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter), for every extern interpretation satisfying the symbolic laws and agreeing with the real primitives.\n\ndef CompRefinesCliBinaryRealL289–302 ↗#Whole-protocol refinement and progress for ELF image bytes at the real primitives: the real primitives obey the symbolic laws (RealPrimsAdmissible); bytes parses and its 18 panic and 5 SampleNTT addresses resolve from .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs); progress holds (CliElfProgressReal); and every guarded execution trace of cliRunElf from initDirs (CliTraces with ValidCall / InputsFor / LeaksFrom, and InvertsGuarded; no RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter under elfRelReal elf addrs) is explained by the composed model or hits a cryptographic collision after an explained prefix.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Refinement.ElfBinding/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Refinement___ElfBinding"}});